2011/6/20 Felipe Gon=E7alves Assis <felipeg.assis@gmail.com>:
> How do you understand {ka makau jei ce'u broda}?

Something, which broda, is such that the truth-value of the
proposition "it broda" is a matter of question.

A classic example of an entity with such a property is "man".

  ro remna cu mrobi'o
  All men die.

  jei ro remna cu mrobi'o
  The truth-value of "All men die."

  makau jei ro remna cu mrobi'o
  Let us ask how "All men die." holds.

  lo remna cu ckaji lo ka makau jei ro ce'u mrobi'o
  Men are such that we can ask how "All of it die." holds.


mu'o mi'e tijlan

